  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Impact Assessment for the Sustainable Development Goals Performance Fund (SDG-PF) Contribution (2015-2023) and Development of Advocacy Document</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The SDG-PF is a pooled fund supporting  underfunded priority areas in relation to Reproductive, Neonatal, Maternal and Child Health (RNMCH) interventions in the health sector in Ethiopia. It is aligned with the Health Sector Development Investment Plan (HSDIP), it is managed by the Federal Ministry of Health and contributions are unearmarked. 
The MOH has requested SDG PF contributors to conduct an impact assessment of the SDG PF funding modality between 2015 and 2023. Different partners have agreed to financially support this request. These include the Bill and Melinda Gates Foundation, Italy, Ireland and the Netherlands. 
This activity consists of two phases: (1) an impact assessment to identify the contributions and attributions of the SDG-PF funding channel in the health sector between 2015 and 2023, divided in two parts, before and after COVID break out, and (2) creating a document that advocates for the advantages and opportunities of this funding channel.</narrative>
  </description>
